From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Smith <scott@newtrostudios.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:36:47 -0400
Subject: remotesmith(0705): server unreachable within 10 s on connects by ID

AC-45 (whole-product review finding 8, the AC-45 part). With the ID server down or
blackholed, a connect by ID waited up to CONNECT_TIMEOUT (18 s) for the rendezvous TCP
connect alone, after DNS/STUN/WebRTC setup, then showed a generic error. Client::start now
bounds only the phase up to the rendezvous connection being up, 10 s from the start of the
connect (the LAN-first attempt included), and ends it with "Server unreachable: ..."; a
rendezvous connect that fails outright (refused, unresolvable, no route) reads the same, with
the OS cause appended. Once the
server answered, punch, relay and data timeouts are upstream's; address routes never use the
server and leave the phase at once. The text says "failed", so a first connect is not
auto-retried, while a dropped session's reconnect streak still retries it.
The absolute 60 s reconnect deadline across in-flight attempts stays deferred.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
